# Linker version script for liblivox_lidar_sdk_shared.so (docker/Dockerfile, checked by docker/test_livox_sdk_symbols.sh).
# The SDK is built with its bundled spdlog 1.3 + fmt; the driver process also loads the system libspdlog 1.12 (ROS logging). With default interposition the dynamic linker bound the SDK's
# `vtable for spdlog::logger`, `typeinfo for spdlog::formatter` ... to the 1.12 copies, so the SDK's global logger (1.3 layout) was destroyed at exit() through the 1.12 vtable and
# livox_ros_driver2_node died with SIGSEGV (-11) in about 1 of 10 shutdowns. Keeping every spdlog/fmt symbol local stops interposition in both directions; the Livox API stays exported.
# The globs are infix on purpose: the symbols to hide include `guard variable for spdlog::...` and std templates carrying spdlog types, which a prefix such as _ZN6spdlog would miss
# (at the pinned SDK commit all 502 hidden symbols mention spdlog or fmt). Only the shared library is covered: the static one still has them, and nothing here links it.
# When LIVOX_SDK2_COMMIT is bumped: diff `nm -D --defined-only` of a build with and without this script and check that everything hidden is spdlog/fmt (an unrelated name containing 3fmt would go too).
{
  global: *;
  local: *6spdlog*; *3fmt*;
};
